## Tools

`config/toolchain.json` pins every tool this project downloads: URL, sha256,
version, license and where the bytes came from. `configure.py` fetches them into
`build/tools/` with `tools/download_tool.py` (standard library only), checking the
sha256 before anything is extracted or run. romwright itself downloads nothing.

* The MWCC PS2 compilers are proprietary, and the ee-gcc builds are third-party
  archives of unverified build provenance (GCC itself is GPL; the bundled Sony and
  SN Systems parts may not be). They are fetched from the decomp.me compilers
  project's release assets; use them only if you are entitled to. Nothing in this
  repository grants that right.
* To use tools you already have, write a toolchain profile (JSON, the format in
  romwright's `docs/toolchains.md`) and pass `python3 configure.py --toolchain profile.json`,
  or save it as `config/toolchain.local.json` (ignored by git). Each tool the
  profile names (`compiler`, `as`, `ld`, `objcopy`, `wibo`, `objdiff-cli`) replaces the
  downloaded one; the rest still come from the manifest.
* `--manifest FILE` substitutes another manifest, e.g. one whose URLs are
  `file://` copies for an offline machine.

## Decompiling a function

Every function is its own `asm/main/NNNN/<name>.s` ({{ASM_UNITS}} of them). To replace one
with C:

```sh
python3 configure.py swap <name-or-0xADDRESS> [--src my_function.c]
# edit src/main/NNNN/<name>.c until `ninja` is green again
```

`swap` changes that function's entry in `config/{{IMAGE}}.yaml` from `asm` to `c`
and creates `src/main/NNNN/<name>.c`; the next `ninja` compiles it into the same
slot of the link. The C file must produce exactly the retail bytes of the function
(it is a whole-function replacement, not an `INCLUDE_ASM` file). `include/romwright_types.h`
has the base types and `include/romwright_protos.h` the prototypes romwright recovered.
`objdiff.json` lists every C unit with its retail target object, so objdiff shows the
difference while you work and `ninja progress` writes `build/report.json`.

## Layout

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `config/{{IMAGE}}.yaml` | splat config: the whole file split into header, code and trailer segments |
| `config/symbol_addrs.txt` | names, addresses and sizes romwright recovered |
| `config/undefined_syms.txt` | absolute names for data the link cannot find an object for |
| `config/checksum.sha1` | the retail sha1 `ninja` checks against |
| `config/project.json` | project facts: image, layout, compiler evidence and flags |
| `include/` | base types and recovered prototypes |
| `src/` | your C units |
| `decompiled/` | optional non-matching reference C from romwright (`--decompile`), not built |
